   "text": "This is a maleimidocaproyl\u2013Val\u2013Lys(sarcosine decamer)\u2013PABC\u2013exatecan drug-linker. I read it in sections from left to right.\n\n- **Maleimide and linker:** A maleimide ring is joined through N to five CH2 groups and then C(=O), which is the 6-maleimidocaproyl unit. It is amide-linked to valine. The valine isopropyl group is on a wedge, which gives L-Val (S).\n- **Lysine:** The Val C(=O) is amide-linked to the lysine \u03b1-NH. The hashed chain bond at the lysine \u03b1-carbon gives L-Lys (S), and the four-CH2 side chain ends in an amide NH.\n- **Sarcosine chain:** The lysine \u03b5-NH is acylated by a chain of 10 N-methylglycine units, N(CH3)CH2C(=O), capped at the N-terminus with acetyl. I counted ten N-methyl nitrogens along the chain.\n- **PABC spacer:** The lysine C(=O) is linked through NH to a para-substituted benzene bearing CH2\u2013O\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH.\n- **Exatecan:** The carbamate NH sits on the wedged benzylic carbon of the tetrahydro ring, which works out to S. That ring is fused to the fluoro-methyl-quinoline, the pyrrolo-pyridone and the lactone. The quaternary carbon carries OH and ethyl on wedges, which gives 20S.\n\nI checked each stereocentre by CIP priority against the drawn wedges and hashes.\n\nSMILES: O=C1C=CC(=O)N1CCCCCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(=O)CN(C)C(=O)CN(C)C(=O)CN(C)C(=O)CN(C)C(=O)CN(C)C(=O)CN(C)C(=O)CN(C)C(=O)CN(C)C(=O)CN(C)C(=O)CN(C)C(C)=O)C(=O)Nc1ccc(COC(=O)N[C@H]2CCc3c(C)c(F)cc4nc5c(c2c34)CN6C(=O)C7=C(C=C56)[C@@](O)(CC)C(=O)OC7)cc1"
